I just got killed wielding one.

I was playing on my laptop (without a numeric keyboard), which I still
have trouble getting used to. I was standing on a chest in a shop on the
left of a shopkeeper.

I am used to looting by pressing "l" for loot, then "y" to the question
whether I want to loot the chest I'm standing on.

Of course, with numberpad set to 0, the "l" key means "move right" (into
the shopkeeper), which was then happily confirmed by pressing "y"...

I managed to kill the shopkeeper, though, mainly because he kept missing
me with his wand, which *did* hit him. *I* also hit him, and when he'd
finally emptied his wand, I could finish him off with my +1 club.

Outside of the shop, I was ambushed by three chickatrices, one of which
left a corpse. I took it, and since I'd already lost my telepathy by
now, I proceeded towards the captain and the other shopkeepers.

I took out a second shopkeeper, the captain of the guard, and the town
priest, and proceeded to the last remaining non-Izchak shopkeeper. I
entered with about 30(80) HP left. What I didn't realise was that
killing four peacefuls had not only removed my telepathy, but also all
of my luck, which would have been at about -10 by now.

Needless to say that I missed, missed, missed, missed, ... with my nice
little chickatrice, until finally the shopkeeper killed me while I was
watching everything but my hit points. I had a wand of teleportation and
a wand of digging with me when I died, and could easily have run away.

Chickatrice' corpses are nice, but don't rely on them if you're fighting
peacefuls...

